WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.820 --> 00:00:04.560
Hello, everybody.
大家好。

2
00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:05.500
Hey there.
大家好。

3
00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:06.720
Guess what?
猜猜怎么着？

4
00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:08.740
My play just opened.
我的话剧刚首演。

5
00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:11.600
Her play just opened and I went for opening night.
她的舞台剧刚首演，我去看了首演之夜。

6
00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:17.860
You did, but you actually haven't done it yet because we're recording this before the play opened.
你是去了，但其实你还没去，因为我们是在话剧上演前录制这一期的。

7
00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:21.520
But I'm hoping that you had a great time and you loved it, lady.
不过我希望你当时玩得很开心，而且你很喜欢，女士。

8
00:00:21.620 --> 00:00:29.900
I'm sure I had a wonderful time and I'm sure you were fantastic and the play was amazing and I probably ate great food in Chicago.
我确信我度过了一段美好的时光，我确信你表现得很棒，话剧非常精彩，而且我可能在芝加哥吃了很棒的食物。

9
00:00:30.740 --> 00:00:33.400
Yeah, what else do you think happened while you were there?
是啊，你觉得你在那里的时候还发生了什么？

10
00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:34.980
Did you meet some wonderful people?
你遇到了一些很棒的人吗？

11
00:00:35.120 --> 00:00:36.960
I introduced you to the cast, I'm sure.
我敢说我一定把你介绍给剧组演员了。

12
00:00:37.260 --> 00:00:42.220
Yeah, I'm also sure I made, you know, really good friends with a perfect stranger at the airport.
是啊，我也敢说我，你知道的，和机场的一个完完全全的陌生人成为了非常要好的朋友。

13
00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:43.320
I'm sure this happened too.
我相信这也发生了。

14
00:00:43.320 --> 00:00:44.060
I tend to do that.
我往往会这样做。

15
00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:48.260
I probably got to know like my cab driver really well, probably know his backstory.
我可能和我的出租车司机聊得很熟，大概还了解了他的背景故事。

16
00:00:48.500 --> 00:00:53.300
Maybe he in another life, you know, before he was a cab driver, did river rafting.
也许他在另一段人生里，你知道的，在他成为出租车司机之前，玩过激流漂流。

17
00:00:53.460 --> 00:00:55.560
I probably got really deep into that conversation.
我可能深入探讨了那个话题。

18
00:00:58.460 --> 00:01:03.100
These are all of our probabilities because we are actually recording this before you go off.
这些都只是我们的猜测，因为我们其实是在你出发前录制这一段的。

19
00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:04.200
And lady, you know what?
而且，女士，你知道吗？

20
00:01:04.360 --> 00:01:08.440
I know we're joking around here, but I am really going to miss you.
我知道我们在这里开玩笑，但我真的很想你。

21
00:01:08.760 --> 00:01:09.160
Aw.
噢。

22
00:01:09.520 --> 00:01:09.900
Yeah.
是啊。

23
00:01:10.180 --> 00:01:11.080
I'm going to miss you.
我会想你的。

24
00:01:11.140 --> 00:01:12.080
I'm going to miss this.
我会想念这一切的。

25
00:01:12.340 --> 00:01:12.960
I know.
我知道。

26
00:01:13.160 --> 00:01:17.140
I think we might need to pop on and do a little Friday chit chat.
我想我们可能得抽空连线，做个简短的周五闲聊。

27
00:01:17.440 --> 00:01:18.400
We have to.
我们必须这么做。

28
00:01:18.540 --> 00:01:20.240
You're going to have all these great Chicago stories.
你会有各种各样精彩的芝加哥故事。

29
00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:21.980
I am going to Iceland.
我要去冰岛。

30
00:01:22.520 --> 00:01:24.620
I am going to the penis museum.
我要去阴茎博物馆。

31
00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:25.240
Yeah.
是啊。

32
00:01:25.360 --> 00:01:27.240
And we're going to need to let people know how that went.
我们需要让大家知道那趟经历怎么样。

33
00:01:27.240 --> 00:01:28.100
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

34
00:01:28.380 --> 00:01:28.880
All right.
好吧。

35
00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:29.620
Well, listen.
听着。

36
00:01:29.880 --> 00:01:30.760
On that note.
借此机会。

37
00:01:30.900 --> 00:01:31.740
On that note.
就着这个话题。

38
00:01:32.180 --> 00:01:33.580
How do we segue here?
我们该怎么承接呢？

39
00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:39.180
Since we're out of town, we wanted to re-air one of our favorite interviews with Zach Woods.
既然我们要出差，我们想重新播放一次我们最喜欢的对扎克·伍兹的采访。

40
00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:41.460
You know he played Gabe Lewis on The Office.
你知道他在《办公室》里扮演过盖比·刘易斯。

41
00:01:41.900 --> 00:01:46.020
He shares with us what it was like to join the show in the middle of season six.
他跟我们分享了在第六季中途加入剧组是什么样的体验。

42
00:01:46.220 --> 00:01:49.320
Plus, we ask him about some of his favorite memories on the show.
此外，我们还问了他关于他在剧中的一些美好回忆。

43
00:01:49.480 --> 00:01:52.680
And then he ends up kind of interviewing us.
然后他最后反过来采访了我们。

44
00:01:52.880 --> 00:01:54.380
It's such a great conversation.
这是一场非常棒的对话。

45
00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:59.020
We hope you enjoy it, and we will see you next week with all new episodes.
我们希望你们会喜欢，我们下周将带着全新单集与大家见面。

46
00:01:59.460 --> 00:01:59.800
All right.
好吧。

47
00:01:59.960 --> 00:02:00.720
Have a good one.
祝你们过得愉快。

48
00:02:04.900 --> 00:02:05.800
I'm Jenna Fisher.
我是珍娜·费舍。

49
00:02:05.980 --> 00:02:07.100
And I'm Angela Kinsey.
我是安吉拉·金赛。

50
00:02:07.220 --> 00:02:08.380
We were on The Office together.
我们曾一起出演过《办公室》。

51
00:02:08.600 --> 00:02:09.620
And we're best friends.
而且我们是最好的朋友。

52
00:02:09.680 --> 00:02:13.460
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office re-watch podcast just for you.
现在，我们专为你们推出了这档终极《办公室》重温播客。

53
00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:17.820
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes
每周，我们都会剖析一集《办公室》，并带来独家幕后故事

54
00:02:17.820 --> 00:02:20.420
stories that only two people who were there can tell you.
只有身临其境的两个人才能讲给你们听的故事。

55
00:02:20.700 --> 00:02:21.600
We're The Office ladies.
我们是办公室女士。

56
00:02:25.460 --> 00:02:25.840
Oh.
哦。

57
00:02:26.060 --> 00:02:26.460
Hey.
嘿。

58
00:02:26.600 --> 00:02:27.360
Welcome back.
欢迎回来。

59
00:02:27.740 --> 00:02:29.100
Welcome back from Thanksgiving.
欢迎感恩节后归来。

60
00:02:29.100 --> 00:02:32.600
We hope everybody had good meals and good times.
我们希望大家都有美味的饭菜和美好的时光。

61
00:02:32.900 --> 00:02:34.520
Yes, with friends and family.
是的，和朋友及家人在一起。

62
00:02:34.760 --> 00:02:36.240
Some people do Friendsgiving.
有些人会过朋友感恩节。

63
00:02:36.680 --> 00:02:40.080
One of my favorite Thanksgivings was a Friendsgiving.
我最喜欢的感恩节之一就是朋友感恩节。

64
00:02:40.280 --> 00:02:42.480
It was my first year in Los Angeles.
那是我去洛杉矶的第一年。

65
00:02:42.640 --> 00:02:44.620
I couldn't afford to fly home to see family.
我买不起机票回家看家人。

66
00:02:44.860 --> 00:02:45.080
Yeah.
是啊。

67
00:02:45.220 --> 00:02:51.120
So me and my other friends who were in L.A., we got together, and we had a Thanksgiving.
所以我和其他在洛杉矶的朋友聚在一起，过了个感恩节。

68
00:02:51.440 --> 00:02:52.940
My friend Luda, she's Russian.
我的朋友露达，她是俄罗斯人。

69
00:02:52.940 --> 00:02:54.700
She brought this Russian vodka.
她带来了这种俄罗斯伏特加。

70
00:02:54.920 --> 00:02:57.260
We all got so hammered.
我们都喝得烂醉如泥。

71
00:02:57.260 --> 00:02:58.380
That's a Friendsgiving.
这才叫朋友感恩节。

72
00:02:58.680 --> 00:03:00.360
It was so fun.
太有趣了。

73
00:03:00.360 --> 00:03:03.060
I actually just found a picture of us recently.
我其实最近刚找到一张我们的合影。

74
00:03:03.060 --> 00:03:04.520
It came up in my memory.
它在我的回忆里弹出来了。

75
00:03:04.900 --> 00:03:05.320
Uh-huh.
嗯哼。

76
00:03:05.580 --> 00:03:05.840
Yeah.
是啊。

77
00:03:06.100 --> 00:03:06.880
I love that.
我太喜欢了。

78
00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:08.040
Yeah, we had traded it.
对，我们把它换了。

79
00:03:08.460 --> 00:03:13.840
You know, Josh, he bought me the most insane thing last year for Thanksgiving.
你知道，乔什去年感恩节给我买了个最疯狂的东西。

80
00:03:13.840 --> 00:03:15.700
And he was like, this is going to be a tradition now.
他说，这以后将成为一个传统。

81
00:03:15.760 --> 00:03:17.080
You're going to have to wear it every Thanksgiving.
你每个感恩节都得穿它。

82
00:03:17.340 --> 00:03:17.900
I was like, babe.
我说，亲爱的。

83
00:03:18.080 --> 00:03:19.000
What is it?
那是什么？

84
00:03:19.080 --> 00:03:19.340
Okay.
好吧。

85
00:03:19.580 --> 00:03:20.660
You know, I'm always cold.
你知道的，我总是怕冷。

86
00:03:21.040 --> 00:03:23.060
And I always want a cozy onesie.
而且我一直想要一套舒服的连体衣。

87
00:03:23.060 --> 00:03:24.460
I'm like, babe, get me a onesie.
我说，亲爱的，给我买套连体衣吧。

88
00:03:24.540 --> 00:03:25.800
Get me a cozy onesie.
给我买套舒服的连体衣。

89
00:03:25.940 --> 00:03:26.180
Okay.
好吧。

90
00:03:26.920 --> 00:03:28.080
Lady, it's a turkey.
天哪，是一只火鸡。

91
00:03:28.300 --> 00:03:29.500
A turkey onesie?
火鸡连体衣？

92
00:03:29.800 --> 00:03:31.700
First of all, it's a one-size-fits-all.
首先，它是均码的。

93
00:03:31.940 --> 00:03:32.980
So it's enormous.
所以它巨大无比。

94
00:03:33.360 --> 00:03:34.240
Do you eat in it?
你穿着它吃饭吗？

95
00:03:34.540 --> 00:03:35.580
Do you wear it all day?
你穿一整天吗？

96
00:03:35.760 --> 00:03:36.580
No, I can't.
不，我不能。

97
00:03:36.620 --> 00:03:39.080
It's like wearing a giant blanket.
就像穿着一条巨大的毯子。

98
00:03:39.860 --> 00:03:42.200
I can't eat in it, but I do put it on.
我没法穿着它吃饭，但我确实会把它穿上。

99
00:03:42.320 --> 00:03:44.020
Well, I've only done—this is my second year.
嗯，我只穿过——这是我的第二年。

100
00:03:44.220 --> 00:03:44.500
Okay.
好吧。

101
00:03:44.680 --> 00:03:47.500
I don't know what the tradition of this turkey onesie is going to be.
我不知道这套火鸡连体衣传统最后会变成什么样。

102
00:03:47.500 --> 00:03:51.360
But I told him, here's what I'll do, because he thinks it's so cute.
但我告诉他，我这样做好啦，因为他觉得这超级可爱。

103
00:03:51.780 --> 00:03:55.580
I put it on, and I watch the Macy's Day Parade in my turkey onesie.
我穿上它，然后穿着火鸡连体衣看梅西感恩节大游行。

104
00:03:55.780 --> 00:03:56.080
Okay.
好吧。

105
00:03:56.660 --> 00:03:57.620
And then, you know—
然后，你知道的——

106
00:03:57.620 --> 00:03:58.280
That sounds cozy.
听起来挺舒服的。

107
00:03:58.300 --> 00:04:02.220
We get the food prep going, but I don't wear it to the actual Thanksgiving dinner.
我们开始准备食物，但我不会穿着它去吃真正的感恩节晚餐。

108
00:04:02.340 --> 00:04:04.640
What is it that Josh thinks is so funny?
乔什觉得哪里好笑了？

109
00:04:04.780 --> 00:04:08.680
I look like a tiny, tiny turkey.
我看起来像一只迷你、迷你的火鸡。

110
00:04:10.280 --> 00:04:11.360
Do you watch football?
你看橄榄球吗？

111
00:04:11.700 --> 00:04:11.800
Oh, yeah.
哦，看。

112
00:04:11.980 --> 00:04:12.900
Football's always on.
总是在播橄榄球。

113
00:04:13.140 --> 00:04:18.280
So when I got into football, I was dating a guy who was from Detroit.
所以我开始看橄榄球的时候，在和一个底特律来的男生交往。

114
00:04:18.540 --> 00:04:20.600
And you know Detroit plays every Thanksgiving.
你知道底特律每年感恩节都会有比赛。

115
00:04:21.060 --> 00:04:21.800
And the Cowboys.
还有牛仔队。

116
00:04:22.100 --> 00:04:22.420
Yes.
对。

117
00:04:22.540 --> 00:04:24.180
Now I'm married to a Dallas man.
现在我嫁给了一个达拉斯男人。

118
00:04:24.320 --> 00:04:24.460
Yeah.
对。

119
00:04:24.640 --> 00:04:25.960
Now I'm a Cowboys fan.
现在我是牛仔队的球迷了。

120
00:04:25.980 --> 00:04:26.400
Oh, yeah.
哦，对。

121
00:04:26.760 --> 00:04:27.060
Yeah.
对。

122
00:04:27.500 --> 00:04:31.320
So Cowboys, every Thanksgiving, you've got to work the meal around it.
所以牛仔队，每个感恩节，你都得绕着它来安排做饭时间。

123
00:04:31.480 --> 00:04:32.860
Half of my family's from Texas.
我有一半家人来自德克萨斯州。

124
00:04:33.060 --> 00:04:33.240
Lady.
天哪。

125
00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:34.040
It's always—
总是——

126
00:04:34.040 --> 00:04:34.480
Yes, you know.
没错，你懂的。

127
00:04:34.560 --> 00:04:35.320
What am I saying?
我在说什么呢？

128
00:04:35.480 --> 00:04:35.920
I know.
我懂。

129
00:04:36.080 --> 00:04:36.600
Of course.
当然。

130
00:04:36.600 --> 00:04:40.720
Well, listen, we have a really exciting show for you today.
好了，听着，我们今天为您准备了一个非常精彩的节目。

131
00:04:41.080 --> 00:04:42.880
I don't even know what to say about it.
我甚至不知道该怎么形容它。

132
00:04:43.060 --> 00:04:46.920
It's maybe one of my favorite episodes we've ever done.
这也许是我们做过的最喜欢的单集之一。

133
00:04:47.480 --> 00:04:50.540
Jenna and I are in love with this interview, you guys.
珍娜和我都爱死这次采访了，伙计们。

134
00:04:50.680 --> 00:04:51.180
I'm sorry.
不好意思。

135
00:04:51.220 --> 00:04:53.480
It's an interview, but it was so wonderful.
虽然这是一场采访，但它太棒了。

136
00:04:53.800 --> 00:04:54.640
Well, Jenna, you tell everyone.
珍娜，你来告诉大家吧。

137
00:04:54.840 --> 00:04:56.560
Well, we got to sit down with Zach Woods.
我们有幸和扎克·伍兹坐在一起聊了聊。

138
00:04:57.100 --> 00:05:00.980
As you know, Zach played Gabe Lewis on 52 episodes of The Office.
如你所知，扎克在《办公室》的52集里饰演了盖比·刘易斯。

139
00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:03.380
He was on from season six to season nine.
他从第六季演到了第九季。

140
00:05:04.100 --> 00:05:05.420
We talk all about it.
我们聊了所有这些。

141
00:05:05.420 --> 00:05:09.360
We talk about his entire time on the show and other things.
我们聊了他在这部剧里的整个经历以及其他事情。

142
00:05:09.680 --> 00:05:10.240
Here's the thing.
关键是这样的。

143
00:05:10.340 --> 00:05:14.020
He's just so interesting, and he's so smart and funny.
他是那么有趣，又那么聪明和滑稽。

144
00:05:14.200 --> 00:05:19.280
And we would be talking about the show, and then he would throw you and I like a curveball question.
我们本来在聊这部剧，然后他会抛给你我一个像这样的突发问题。

145
00:05:19.480 --> 00:05:25.640
Like a deep, light question about what it means to be just human and alive.
一个深奥却轻松的问题，关于作为一个有血有肉的人意味着什么。

146
00:05:25.740 --> 00:05:26.020
Yes.
是的。

147
00:05:26.020 --> 00:05:27.020
Like, so fun.
真是太好玩了。

148
00:05:27.460 --> 00:05:30.280
Oh, I just can't wait for everyone to listen to this interview.
哦，我简直迫不及待想让大家听听这次采访了。

149
00:05:30.280 --> 00:05:31.320
I just love it.
我太喜欢了。

150
00:05:31.760 --> 00:05:37.520
Well, you guys, Zach is currently working on a new stop-motion animation series called In the Know.
各位，扎克目前正在制作一部名为《知情者》的新定格动画系列。

151
00:05:37.720 --> 00:05:40.940
He's the co-creator, the director, and star of the show.
他是这部节目的共同创作者、导演兼主演。

152
00:05:41.100 --> 00:05:45.220
And Greg Daniels is one of the executive producers, so you know this is going to be good.
而格雷格·丹尼尔斯是执行制片人之一，所以你知道这绝对错不了。

153
00:05:45.620 --> 00:05:48.800
The show premieres on Peacock in the new year, so be on the lookout.
这部剧将在新年的Peacock平台上首播，大家敬请期待。

154
00:05:49.300 --> 00:05:51.080
Yeah, we'll share about it in stories.
对，我们会在快拍里分享的。

155
00:05:51.080 --> 00:05:51.980
But you know what?
但你知道吗？

156
00:05:51.980 --> 00:05:56.520
I think we take a quick break and get to this interview because it's so fantastic.
我想我们先休息一下，直接进入今天的采访，因为真的太精彩了。

157
00:05:56.520 --> 00:05:57.500
You're going to love it.
你们一定会喜欢的。

158
00:05:57.600 --> 00:06:01.100
And the second half, dare I say, is even better than the firSt.
而且后半部分，我敢说，比前半部分还要精彩。

159
00:06:01.280 --> 00:06:02.740
It keeps getting better and better.
真是越来越精彩了。

160
00:06:03.260 --> 00:06:03.960
Here it is.
马上开始。

161
00:06:15.660 --> 00:06:16.100
Hello.
你好。

162
00:06:16.540 --> 00:06:18.440
Zach, how wonderful to see you.
扎克，见到你太高兴了。

163
00:06:18.640 --> 00:06:20.440
